-----------------------------------------------The starred programs -- what they need and where they are------------------------------------------------------The starred programs sit in /dd/CMDS and /dd/CMDS/GAMES with everythingelse; the star before the name is what tells them apart, rather than adirectory of their own.Each was compiled `cc -qixm`: the C library lives in Microware's `cio`trap handler rather than being linked in, which made for small binariesand was the normal way to build for OS-9.  `cio`, `csl` and `math` shipin /dd/CMDS by Microware's permission, so the starred programs run asthey are; DOC/README-CIO has the details.DOC/README-CIO explains the three ways to set this up.All 335, verified by running every program on this disk with no cio present:  adduser         alps            answer          aprocs  ar2             areacode        arepdaemon      as09  ascii           atp             autolf          autoreply  back            backgammon      banner          basename  bcheck          bdecode         blackjak        bmg  boa             bootgen         bootlogger      booz  byteflip        c7decode        cal             calender  cam             cat             cb              cccp2  ccheck          charcnt         chbase          checkalias  checkenv        checkfile       checksum        chgrp  chksum          chown           ckermit         clear  colortest       combine         connect         cp  cpu             cpucache        cribbage        crontab  crypto          cuts            cxref           cyberwar  dam             dbz             dc              dclock  delbak          des             detab           dfiles  dhryGcc         dhryGcc2        dhryGcc2in      dhryGcc2mx  dhryGcc2o2      dhryGccin       dhryGccmx       dhryGcco2  dhryshamu       dhryshamu2      diff            digclk  dinfo           dir             dirname         disable  divide          dld             dload           dm  dmake 