ur with `3,4d6', a repeat                 with `2@'; with nothing it rolls d100  showpic       show a picture on the Atari GRAPH display.  With the                `graph' trap library resident it is entered and aborts: it                wants the display, not just the library.  reversi        Othello against the computer or another player at the same                 keyboard, with six strengths from Apprentice to Very Hard.                 It opens on a menu; the arrow keys or hjkl move the cursor,                 RETURN places a disk and `m' reopens the menu.  `-r' resumes                 a saved game.  A different author's program from `othello'  sine           a sine plot on the Atari Graph display; it calls the `graph'                 trap library  ski            Ski! -- down an endless slope a row a turn: R and L turn, J                 jumps, T teleports, I fires at the Snoman; Return waits  sol            Klondike solitaire at the terminal: t thumbs the deck three                 cards at a time, m moves a card or a run, h lists the                 commands and q quits  solx           a harder solitaire with no deck: every card is dealt into                 runs, which may be split -- `m run position destination';                 h lists the commands *striche        line drawing for the Atari Graph display; it calls the                 `graph' trap library, so load that first  thricken       collect every diamond on the screen and the next level loads:                 hjkl move, s and r save and restore the level, q leaves and                 ^C quits; -l <n> starts at level n and -d plays a set of                 screens of your own.  Screens in GAMES/THRICKEN; DOC/thricken  torus          robots on a torus: each move you make, the robots close in --                 lead them into each other to make scrap heaps; hjklyubn                 move, t teleports, q quits; scores in GAMES/TORUS  trek73         Star Trek battle at a Code [